<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) RAISES GASOLINE PRICES.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) RAISES GASOLINE PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will increase gasoline prices by 0.20 drachmas per litre, effective on Thursday.</p>
<p>Heating fuel prices will be increased by 0.90 drachmas and transport diesel by 0.40 drachmas per litre, it said.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after world gasoline prices rose $2.0 per metric tonne and heating oil and diesel prices by $4.0 and $2.4 per metric tonne and a lower dollar/drachma exchange rate, down 1.24 drachmas per $, DEP said. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
